@* Shared by Product/EditProduct and Downloads/Index (#1550): one wording for the Linux probe install hint. *@
<p class="text-muted small">For a Linux host, <b>Download Linux probe</b> gives a <code>.tar.gz</code> with the probe package, its config (this server's address) and the access key in a separate file. Run <code>tar xzf hsm-linux-probe-&lt;product&gt;.tar.gz &amp;&amp; sudo ./hsm-linux-probe-&lt;product&gt;/install.sh</code> on the host; the probe installs as a systemd service and connects. <b>One product per Linux host:</b> the probe reports at the product root with no host node (<code>.computer/…</code> and <code>.probe/…</code>), so installing the same product's bundle on a second host mixes both hosts' values into the same sensors — create a product per host.</p>
